---

## The Real Problem

**Question answered:**
Can ML reduce high-error inventory decision
weeks from 18% to under 10% across 45 stores
— replacing Monday morning guessing with a
quantified confidence range per store?

At naive last-week forecasting:
- Errors exceed 10% in 18% of weeks
- Average error $79,126 per store weekly
- Stockout or overstock risk every 5th week

At our model:
- Errors exceed 10% in 7% of weeks
- Average error $38,661 per store weekly
- Risk halved — every 14th week

