## 8-Step ML Roadmap

### Step 1 — Business Problem
- 45 stores, $263K to $2.55M — 10x spread
- MAPE below 5%, R² above 0.95
- Dataset: closed Kaggle competition
- Baselines: three rule-based, no leaderboard

### Step 2 — Data and EDA
- 6,435 rows, zero nulls, zero duplicates
- 5 statistical tests before any modelling
- Key finding: Christmas week BELOW average
  (December 28th = post-Christmas decline)

### Step 3 — Feature Engineering
- 8 raw → 33 features
- 95% of improvement from this step
- lag_52 = #1 SHAP, $800K impact
- Cyclic encoding, holiday interactions

### Step 4 — Split
- Chronological 70/15/15
- Random split rejected — data leakage

### Step 5 — Model Selection
- 4 models compared: DT, RF, XGB, LightGBM
- MAPE used for selection — non-normal data,
  10x store size range, RMSE unfair
- LightGBM selected

### Step 6 — Evaluation
- MAPE, MAE, RMSE, R², WMAE calculated
- Three baselines compared
- SHAP explainability implemented
- 100% of 45 stores improved
- All high-error predictions documented

### Step 7 — Deployment
- 6-page live Streamlit dashboard
- Real-time prediction with confidence ranges
- Store bias warnings, prediction logging

### Step 8 — Monitoring
- 0 of 21 months triggered 8% alert
- Drift detection — 4 economic variables
- 4 retraining triggers defined

